// The last bytes that a program writes to stdout are not a newline. The
// bootstrap wrapper must pass them on: "abc" reaches stdout, with no newline
// after it. A wrapper that reads the output line by line can drop such a last
// line (issue #634). The JVM backend cannot open /dev/stdout on a pipe, so
// only the bootstrap gate runs this probe.
var out = open("/dev/stdout", "w");
out.write("abc");
out.close();

// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: abc
